# oracle: pair_style meam, two-element CsCl (lattce(1,2) = b2) alloy (w37meam_lib.meam + w37meam_b2.meam, zbl 0, nn2 = 0), 3x3x3 cells of 2 atoms (54 atoms; A on the simple cubic corners, B at the body centres), lattice constant 2 re(1,2)/sqrt(3) = 3.002221 A (nearest-neighbour distance re(1,2) = 2.6 A), 0.04 A sinusoidal displacement, velocities from atom-style variables, fix nve, 30 steps of 0.001 ps
# oracle: the eight unlike neighbours at 2.6 A form the first shell; the like neighbours at 3.002221 A are inside the cutoff and keep the crystal off the Rose energy; pair distances stay in [2.4, 3.8] A, away from the cutoff window [3.9, 4.0]
# oracle-inputs: w37meam_lib.meam w37meam_b2.meam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-6 abs=1e-9
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
variable        a equal 3.002221
lattice         custom ${a} a1 1 0 0 a2 0 1 0 a3 0 0 1 &
                basis 0 0 0 basis 0.5 0.5 0.5
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box basis 1 1 basis 2 2
mass            1 63.546
mass            2 58.69
variable        dx atom 0.04*sin(2.3*x+1.1*y+0.4*z)
variable        dy atom 0.04*cos(1.9*y-0.7*x+0.3*z)
variable        dz atom 0.04*sin(1.3*z+0.8*x-0.5*y)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
variable        vx atom 0.4*cos(1.7*y-0.6*z)
variable        vy atom 0.4*sin(1.2*z+0.9*x)
variable        vz atom 0.3*cos(2.1*x-0.8*y+0.2)
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz units box
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * w37meam_lib.meam A B w37meam_b2.meam A B
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve
thermo          10
thermo_style    custom step pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             30
